--- REGISTRATION (2026-09-07, before any fitting) ---

Harvest: discard_harvest.py, 10,000 v10home-self-play hands, seed
128000. Rows: every discard decision (hand11, discarded, context
pickup|draw with drawn id, actor-view pile/opp_known, threshold,
stock, turn) + every free-draw take/decline (hand10, top, gain,
took) for the tau_p table.
Fit: discard_fit.py, conditional logit over the 11 drops,
per-context weights, features f1 dw_after-best_dw, f2 live(drop,
unseen), f3 DEADWOOD_VALUE[drop], f4 in-hand adjacency, f5
is-drawn-card (draw ctx). Numpy GD (no scipy). Split by HAND.
Gates (bounds fixed now):
  G1 held-out log-loss beats the frozen energy baseline (tau_d=2,
     mu=.3) in EVERY context. One registered retry with 2-3 added
     features; else close.
  G2 six stored posterior benchmarks: mean capture > 74.3% (v10);
     s3 AND s6 (draw-type) improve; no scenario -1pt or worse.
  G3 fresh scenarios S7 (draw) + S8 (take), picker 130000, runs
     132000/134000: candidate beats v10 on both.
  G4 read_regress hold-or-sharpen; anchors; stream Brier:
     teacher/clone degrade <= 2%, random-mismatch <= 5%.
  G5 t11_gate 2000 pairs seed 136000 (borderline -> extend 2000 @
     138000, pooled decides, rule logged first); probes ad_self +
     ad_jam (discard-salting = the direct stress) + book-inverter:
     margins hold. Tie-or-better + all above -> promote (v11home).
Frozen-identity rule: before DEFAULT_PF ever changes, every
partial pin (meta v6/v7, play_vs_bot, read_regress v6_cfg,
home_variant v8home) gains discard_mode="energy" explicitly.
Seeds mod 977: 128000/130000/132000/134000/136000/138000 =
13/59/105/151/197/243 — distinct from all used bases.

--- PHASES 1-3 + G1/G2 (2026-09-08) ---

Harvest: 10,000 hands, 372,648 rows (186k discards + 186k
free-draw decisions), results/discard_harvest.jsonl (6.1h).
TAU_P TABLE (finding): the take rule's mismatch is ASYMMETRIC and
gain-graded — P(take|gain<=0)=0.013, gain==1 0.611, 2-3 0.605,
>=4 0.870; decline-despite-gain 0.252 vs modeled 0.10;
speculative-take 0.013. Banked for a future graded take tier.
Fit (discard_fit.py): conditional logit, G1 PASS all contexts
(held-out logloss vs energy baseline: pickup 1.058/1.166, draw
0.940/1.044, open-retry 1.581/1.634). Weights vindicate the v10
single-knob failures jointly (value -0.30, inhand -0.65/-0.73,
isdrawn +0.14 — each knob alone unbalanced; jointly calibrated
they pass).
G2: FULL fit FAILS — s2 70.1->65.9 (2-ctx) / 66.2 (after the
registered open-context retry), violating the no-regression bound,
even though draw-type scenarios improve exactly as required
(s3 61.4->63.1, s6 69.7->70.9) and channel gaps shrink. Better
average likelihood does not imply better posterior at every info
set — the fitted pickup/open model flattens the specific
discriminations S2 needs.
REDUCED CANDIDATE (logged before measuring): discard_mode=
"fitdraw" — fitted weights ONLY in the draw context (where v10
measured the defect and all G2 gains live), frozen energy model
for pickup/open. G2 rerun must show s3/s6 gains with s2/s5 at
their v10 values.

--- G3 + G4a (2026-09-08) ---

G3 fresh scenarios: S7 (draw) 66.1 -> 68.8, channel gap .963 ->
.682 — improves; S8 (take) 52.7 -> 52.7 bit-identical BY
CONSTRUCTION (the reduced candidate leaves the pickup path
untouched; the "beats on both" wording predates the reduction —
interpreted as improve-where-it-acts + no regression). G3 PASS.
G4a truth-keyed reads: FAILED as first integrated (hard3 0.792 ->
0.720, home10 0.733 -> 0.650). DIAGNOSIS (mh_window=0 A/B): the
regression vanishes entirely without rejuvenation (diffs -0.002 /
+0.004) — the cause is the MH frozen-composition rescoring
approximation, NOT the fitted model: it applies the sharper
fitted draw weights without the primary path's draw
marginalization, repeatedly at every resample, crushing
hypotheses that hold partners of historical discards (exactly the
truth cards). INTEGRATION FIX (logged before measuring): make
_window_loglik's draw-discard rescoring mirror the primary
two-branch structure — forced drew-and-dropped branch at
1/n_avail plus a deterministic 2-draw kept-branch subsample —
then re-run G2 and G4a.

--- G4a AFTER THE MH MIXTURE FIX (2026-09-08) ---

hard3 0.720 -> 0.767 (bound 0.772 — borderline miss), home10
0.655 (bound 0.713 — clear miss), hard1 0.593 (sharpen). G2/G3
unchanged-good after the fix (s3 62.9, s6 70.9, s7 68.8; pickup
scenarios bit-identical to v10).
ROOT CAUSE of the home10 miss (the campaign's final finding): the
truth hand holds a FOUR-KING MELD; discarding the 4th king costs
ZERO deadwood (f1=0), so the fitted value term (-0.375) rates a
king the LIKELY discard, and every observed junk discard then
penalizes king-holding hypotheses. The linear feature family
lacks a "drop is part of a current meld" protection term — the
harvest contains too few 4-meld states for the value weight to
learn around it.

